@startuml
' CanadaLogin Partner Portal - C4 level 4 code view.
'
' Work context: local illustrative sample only.
' Source codebase: ../gc-signin-partner-portal, read as source material only.
' View question: which code elements implement the workspace/RP application
' invitation and application-management slice?
' Excluded: every route, every CRUD adapter, frontend component internals,
' complete database schema, and runtime sequence details.

left to right direction
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam wrapWidth 180
hide circle

title CanadaLogin Partner Portal - C4 Level 4 Code View: Workspace And RP Application Slice

package "backend/src/app/api/v1" {
  class "workspaces.py\nFastAPI router" as WorkspacesRouter <<module>> {
    +create_workspace()
    +list_current_user_workspaces()
    +invite_rp_application_developer()
    +accept_rp_application_developer_invitation()
    +create_rp_application()
    +update_rp_application()
    +get_rp_application_usage_summary()
  }
}

package "backend/src/app/services" {
  class WorkspaceService <<service>> {
    +create_workspace(...)
    +list_current_user_workspaces(...)
    +create_rp_application(...)
    +update_rp_application(...)
    +invite_rp_application_developer(...)
    +accept_rp_application_developer_invitation(...)
    +get_rp_application_usage_summary(...)
    +get_rp_application_client_credentials(...)
    -_get_workspace_admin_rp_application(...)
    -_create_rp_application_developer_invitation(...)
    -_get_current_user_rp_application_context(...)
    -_hash_invitation_token(raw_token)
    -_build_rp_application_invite_url(raw_token)
  }

  class IBMVerifyAdminService <<service>> {
    +build_application_creation_payload(...)
    +build_application_update_payload(...)
    +normalize_usage_and_audit_payloads(...)
  }

  class GCNotifyService <<service>> {
    +send_email(recipient_email, personalisation, reference)
  }
}

package "backend/src/app/repositories" {
  class "crud_workspaces" as WorkspaceCrud <<FastCRUD>>
  class "crud_workspace_members" as WorkspaceMemberCrud <<FastCRUD>>
  class "crud_application_infos" as ApplicationInfoCrud <<FastCRUD>>
  class "crud_application_contacts" as ApplicationContactCrud <<FastCRUD>>
  class "crud_rp_applications" as RPApplicationCrud <<FastCRUD>>
  class "crud_rp_application_developer_invitations" as InvitationCrud <<FastCRUD>>
  class "crud_users" as UserCrud <<FastCRUD>>
  class IBMVerifyAdminClient <<HTTP client>> {
    +create_application(payload)
    +update_application(application_id, payload)
    +get_client_secret(client_id)
    +update_client_secret(client_id, payload)
    +get_application_total_logins(application_id, from_date, to_date)
    +get_application_audit_trail(application_id, from_date, to_date, size, sort_by, sort_order)
  }
}

package "backend/src/app/models" {
  class Workspace <<SQLAlchemy model>> {
    +id
    +uuid
    +name
    +slug
    +department_id
    +created_by
  }

  class WorkspaceMember <<SQLAlchemy model>> {
    +workspace_id
    +user_id
    +role
  }

  class ApplicationInfo <<SQLAlchemy model>> {
    +workspace_id
    +name
  }

  class ApplicationContact <<SQLAlchemy model>> {
    +application_info_id
  }

  class RPApplication <<SQLAlchemy model>> {
    +workspace_id
    +application_info_id
    +name
    +uuid
    +ibm_sv_application_id
    +status
  }

  class RPApplicationDeveloperInvitation <<SQLAlchemy model>> {
    +workspace_id
    +rp_application_id
    +invited_email
    +token_hash
    +invite_expires_at
    +invited_by
    +role
    +accepted_at
    +revoked_at
    +gc_notify_notification_id
  }

  class User <<SQLAlchemy model>> {
    +id
    +uuid
    +email
    +auth_provider
    +auth_subject
  }
}

package "backend/src/app/schemas" {
  class WorkspaceCreate <<Pydantic schema>>
  class RPApplicationCreate <<Pydantic schema>>
  class RPApplicationUpdate <<Pydantic schema>>
  class RPApplicationDeveloperInvitationCreate <<Pydantic schema>>
  class RPApplicationDeveloperInvitationRead <<Pydantic schema>>
  class RPApplicationCurrentUserRead <<Pydantic schema>>
}

WorkspacesRouter --> WorkspaceService : Depends(get_workspace_service)
WorkspacesRouter ..> WorkspaceCreate
WorkspacesRouter ..> RPApplicationCreate
WorkspacesRouter ..> RPApplicationUpdate
WorkspacesRouter ..> RPApplicationDeveloperInvitationCreate
WorkspacesRouter ..> RPApplicationDeveloperInvitationRead
WorkspacesRouter ..> RPApplicationCurrentUserRead

WorkspaceService --> WorkspaceCrud : create/get/update/delete
WorkspaceService --> WorkspaceMemberCrud : membership checks
WorkspaceService --> ApplicationInfoCrud : application info records
WorkspaceService --> ApplicationContactCrud : contact records
WorkspaceService --> RPApplicationCrud : RP application records
WorkspaceService --> InvitationCrud : invitation create/get/update
WorkspaceService --> UserCrud : invited/current user lookups
WorkspaceService --> IBMVerifyAdminService : IBM app, credentials, usage, audit
WorkspaceService --> GCNotifyService : invitation email

IBMVerifyAdminService --> IBMVerifyAdminClient : call admin endpoints
InvitationCrud --> RPApplicationDeveloperInvitation : persists
RPApplicationCrud --> RPApplication : persists
WorkspaceCrud --> Workspace : persists
WorkspaceMemberCrud --> WorkspaceMember : persists
ApplicationInfoCrud --> ApplicationInfo : persists
ApplicationContactCrud --> ApplicationContact : persists
UserCrud --> User : persists

RPApplicationDeveloperInvitation --> Workspace : workspace_id
RPApplicationDeveloperInvitation --> RPApplication : rp_application_id
RPApplicationDeveloperInvitation --> User : invited_by
RPApplication --> Workspace : workspace_id
RPApplication --> ApplicationInfo : application_info_id
ApplicationContact --> ApplicationInfo : application_info_id
WorkspaceMember --> Workspace : workspace_id
WorkspaceMember --> User : user_id

note right of WorkspaceService
  Focused code view for the partner-specific slice.
  It shows modules/classes and persistence relationships,
  not a runtime sequence or full database ERD.
end note

@enduml
